# Diagnostics' pages: the loader's CRC line fits (v0.3.2: it and the cart
# page's WAITCNT line ran off the edge; diag_say now wraps a long line), the
# clock page says it is measuring before its 2-second wait, and the EEPROM
# page speaks to users. (The cart page shows the build ID, which changes
# with the code.)
# Diagnostics from L+R+SELECT held at power-on (diag-back starts it from Info), A
# once its first page is up and those keys are let go
-k 1:L+R+SELECT
-w "screen ready: diag-start"
-k 60:-
-k @40:A -k @44:-
-w "diag: measuring the clock"
-s @10:clock.png
-w "diag: boot loader present: pass"
-s @10:loader.png
-w "diag: B, each time"
-s @10:eeprom.png
